   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro Memorial Bridge",
    "basePrintNo": "S7224",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7224-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-m, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7224\n\nSPONSOR: SERINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro Memorial\nBridge\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo honor Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro by designating a portion of the\nstate highway as the \"Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro Memorial Bridge\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law to designate the bridge across the\nTaconic state parkway on Pudding Street, in the town of Putnam Valley as\nthe \"Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2: Provides that the Commissioner of Transportation shall\nprovide for the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the\nstate highway system as designated pursuant to section 1 of this act.\nProvided, however, that the designation shall be one of ceremonial\nnature and the official name of such bridge shall not be changed as a\nresult of this act.\n\nSection 3: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nBoth Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro contributed significantly to the Putnam\nValley community they called home for years. Both served in the United\nStates Military-Jim in the Marines and Joseph in the Navy-as well as in\nthe Putnam Valley Volunteer Fire Department. Jim Gordon also served his\ncommunity as a member of the Putnam Valley Free Library Board, Town\nZoning Board of Appeals and County Legislator, including serving as the\nChairman of the Legislature.  Joseph Marro also further served his\ncommunity, including as a member of the Knights of Columbus, the school\nboard, the Town Council, the library board of trustees, and Putnam Coun-\nty Traffic Safety Board and serving as PTA Board President.\n\nBoth these individuals continued giving back to their community until\ntheir passing as volunteers for numerous not-for-profit groups and\nhelped improve the lives of so many around them. This legislation would\ncommemorate their endeavors by designating the Taconic Overpass at\nPudding Street as the \"Jim Gordon and Joseph Marro Memorial Bridge\" in\ntheir honor.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
