    "lawCode": "Add §344-n, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7224A\n\nSPONSOR: SERINO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Putnam Valley First Responders Bridge\"\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo honor Putnam Valley First Responders by designating a portion of the\nstate highway as the \"Putnam Valley First Responders Bridge\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law to designate the bridge across the\nTaconic state parkway on Pudding Street, in the town of Putnam Valley as\nthe \"Putnam Valley First Responders Bridge\".\n\nSection 2: Provides that the Commissioner of Transportation shall\nprovide for the installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the\nstate highway system as designated pursuant to section 1 of this act.\nProvided, however, that the designation shall be one of ceremonial\nnature and the official name of such bridge shall not be changed as a\nresult of this act:\n\nSection 3: Provides the date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPutnam Valley first responders are an integral part of the Putnam Valley\ncommunity. First responders put their lives on the line daily to serve\nand protect Putnam Valley, and it was thanks in part to their efforts\nand push for change that the long awaited Pudding Street Overpass became\na reality. This bill seeks to honor and recognize the service Putnam\nValley first responders provide to our community by naming a heavily\ntraversed bridge in their honor, so that drivers are readily reminded of\ntheir service and sacrifice.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
